al-khaser with a code per check, for alkhaser_search.sh (evasion-tests/README.md)

Upstream: https://github.com/ayoubfaouzi/al-khaser (GPL-2.0), applies to commit
f0e5559073fe02c4f50cc8c3ed8d5b302a6a0659. build_al_khaser.sh clones that commit and applies
this file; its hunks keep al-khaser's CRLF line endings (see .gitattributes here).

- Every check reports a code, category * 1000 + its position in the category (TLS 1 ...
  ANALYSIS_TOOLS 15, HUMAN_INTERACTION 16), on its result line and in log.txt.
- The exit code is the first detection. Each detection also ends a thread with its code, and
  each check's start, detection and block is marked with an event named
  "al-khaser <code> <category|start|detected|blocked> <text>", so a DRAKVUF syscall trace names
  them (NtTerminateThread, NtCreateEvent).
- Each check runs on its own thread: one that has not returned within --check-timeout
  (default 120 s) is reported as blocked, code 100000 + its code, and the run goes on.
- The human-interaction checks (mouse movement, user input) are off by default; getchar()
  only with --pause.

